    "created_at": "2019-05-10T13:39:01Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-05-10T13:39:01Z",
    "body": "I can understand the reasoning on the bug: some platforms may have a convention that the appearance of an on-screen keyboard always causes the input to scroll into view. This is a separate mechanism from the focus causing the input to scroll into view.\r\n\r\nI think the path here would be to clarify in the focus() spec that although preventScroll would prevent any scrolling due to focus, it wouldn't prevent any scrolling due to other actions, such as the user dragging the screen, or accessibility technology, or on-screen keyboards appearing.",
